rate and the 3rd highest screen rate in the league. Aaron Rodgers has run the passing game, with DK Metcalf leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Steelers defense has been well above average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per play, where it ranks 8th, and it has no real weak spot. Alex Highsmith has led the way with 3 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a number of defenders in the box that ranks 7th highest in the league.","special":"The Steelers have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 80% of field goals, which is a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into linebackers, about 31% of the money on the books. Their linebackers were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Aaron Rodgers has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,699 yards. DK Metcalf has been the clear top target with 24% of the looks and 374 receiving yards. Jaylen Warren has handled most of the work in the backfield with 70% of the carries. On defense, T.J. Watt leads the team with 5.5 sacks.","coaching":"Mike McCarthy is calling the offense as head coach and Patrick Graham is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Seahawks and the 2023 Bengals under Zac Taylor. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Titans under Dennard Wilson and the 2023 Raiders under Patrick Graham.","trends":"The offense went from 16th in EPA per play in 2025 to 25th so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 18th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 8th so far this season, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 4% to 13%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}